      "problem": "What is $\\frac{3x+9z}{6x-15z}$ reduced to its lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+9z}{6x-15z} & =\\frac{3(x+3z)}{3(2x-5z)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\cdot (x+3z)}{\\cancel{3}\\cdot (2x-5z)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3z}{2x-5z}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
